.TH BIALET 1 "2026-11-09" "bialet" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bialet \- full-stack web framework with embedded Wren and SQLite
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bialet
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIAPPDIR\fR]
.br
.B bialet dev
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bialet
serves the application directory as a web site. Each
.I .wren
file in the directory is a route handler that returns a response body. The
server, the Wren interpreter, and an SQLite database live in one binary, with
no configuration files and no separate runtime.
.PP
With no arguments it serves the current directory on 127.0.0.1:7001. The
argument after the options, if given, selects a different application
directory.
.PP
The subcommand
.B dev
enables live reload and the in-browser error display, and opens the server URL
in a browser. The flags are stored in the database and persist across restarts.
.PP
Bialet speaks HTTP/1.0 and does not terminate TLS. Put nginx, Apache, or Caddy
in front for HTTPS, HTTP/2, and rate limiting.
.SH OPTIONS
Every option has a short and a long form; values may be passed as
\fB\-\-option value\fR or \fB\-\-option=value\fR.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " \fIPORT\fR"
Port to listen on. Default: 7001.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-host " \fIHOST\fR"
Host name or address to bind. Default: 127.0.0.1.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-run " \fICODE\fR"
Run the Wren code passed as the argument, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-validate " \fIFILE\fR"
Validate the syntax of a Wren file, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-tests
Run the tests in the \fI_tests/\fR folder.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-log " \fIFILE\fR"
Write the log to a file instead of standard output.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-db " \fIFILE\fR"
SQLite database file. Default: \fI_db.sqlite3\fR.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-wal
Enable SQLite write-ahead logging.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-ignore " \fIGLOBS\fR"
Comma-separated list of glob patterns of files to ignore.
Default: \fIREADME*,AGENTS*,LICENSE*,*.json,*.yml,*.yaml\fR.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mem\-soft " \fIMB\fR"
Soft memory limit in MB. Default: 128.
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-mem\-hard " \fIMB\fR"
Hard memory limit in MB. Default: 256.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-cpu\-soft " \fIPERCENT\fR"
Soft CPU limit in percent. Default: 15.
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-cpu\-hard " \fIPERCENT\fR"
Hard CPU limit in percent. Default: 30.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-max\-post " \fIKB\fR"
Maximum request body size in KB. Default: 128.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-max\-upload\-size " \fISIZE\fR"
Maximum size per uploaded file in bytes; a
.B K
,
.B M
, or
.B G
suffix scales it. Default: 4M.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-foreign\-keys " \fION|OFF\fR"
SQLite foreign key enforcement. Default: on.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-synchronous " \fILEVEL\fR"
SQLite synchronous mode: off, normal, full, or extra. Default: normal.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress the browser auto-open and colored output.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run the application in the current directory:
.PP
.nf
.RS
bialet
.RE
.fi
.PP
Serve another directory on all interfaces, port 8080:
.PP
.nf
.RS
bialet \-h 0.0.0.0 \-p 8080 /path/to/app
.RE
.fi
.PP
Start in development mode:
.PP
.nf
.RS
bialet dev
.RE
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I _db.sqlite3
Default SQLite database, created next to the application files.
.SH SEE ALSO
Documentation at https://bialet.dev.
